      "closure_rationale": "Nested expansion preserves complete caller argument tokens while allocating one fresh context per invocation. A concrete reverse environment resolves the caller identity to11 and an original retagged or symbol-only defect to99. Namespace authority and context equality are explicit caller/runtime contracts, not unforgeable C types. Two-list zip and independent-list nested repetitions have explicit binding indices separate from syntax contexts. Per-invocation freshness, MAX sentinel exhaustion and depth/token/instruction limits are derived; zero-output recursion still consumes work. Actual Rust2021 positives and three translation refusals distinguish mixed-site lookup, unequal repetition and cross-invocation scope from this smaller uniform-context language. Six profiles pass four named anchors, eight compiled semantic controls including actual retained MOD17/18, and four compiling learner stubs reject. An independent explicit-work-stack oracle matches13720cases:2416successes,5400structural refusals,865shape refusals,4024budget refusals,794exhaustions and221capture refusals. Exact output and context authority remain unchanged on failures after partial work. Required nested macros, equal-length metavariables, independent nested repetition, explicit parent-context escapes and three resource budgets are fully implemented and executed. Real Rust comparison supplies definition-site local/invocation-site item and explicit identifier-binding counterexamples; no full Rust/ISO C macro equivalence is claimed. All13cost rows, actual compiler object/stack observations and seven equal-contract samples are present; unaided delayed assessment remains external. Bounded author support only."
